Cell[TextData[{
 "The reduced correlator G[] appearing in the four-point function will depend \
on full super-cross-ratios, not only on \[Chi] and \[Zeta]. At the bosonic \
limit, the algebra will just be direct sum of Conformal algebra and \
R-symmetry algebra. The supercharges make it truly \
\[OpenCurlyQuote]super-conformal\[CloseCurlyQuote]. So G[\[Chi]F, \[Zeta]F] \
can be expanded in G[\[Chi], \[Zeta]] + nilpotent terms. This series will \
terminate at finite order, and while doing this expansion, we need to \
evaluate the expression ",
 StyleBox["taylor",
  FontFamily->"Californian FB",
  FontWeight->"Light"],
 StyleBox[" ",
  FontFamily->"Californian FB"],
 "that is Grassmann analogue of ",
 StyleBox["Series[G[\[Chi] + \[Delta]\[Chi], \[Zeta] + \[Delta]\[Zeta]], {\
\[Delta]\[Chi], 0, nilpotency order}, {\[Delta]\[Zeta], 0, nilpotency order}]",
  FontFamily->"Californian FB",
  FontWeight->"Normal"],
 ".  We define the helper function ",
 StyleBox["gMul[]",
  FontFamily->"Californian FB",
  FontWeight->"Normal"],
 " and ",
 StyleBox["gPow[]",
  FontFamily->"Californian FB",
  FontWeight->"Normal"],
 " first."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9770559825253105`*^9, 3.9770560639994755`*^9}, {
  3.9770561045143013`*^9, 3.9770561815369873`*^9}, {3.9770565365904408`*^9, 
  3.977056626352356*^9}, {3.9770567027505608`*^9, 
  3.9770567259828415`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"7e8c4554-b2f3-cc4d-9c99-\
7b80530ee73d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gPow", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
